nesses, coverage gaps, risks, classification of author-test failure, positive control classification, verdict rationale.\n\nBoth must be mandatory. Let me write them.\n\nCounts:\n- independent_probe_counts: {\"tests\": 4, \"passed\": 4, \"failed\": 0, \"errors\": 0, \"skipped\": 0, \"exit_code\": 0, \"elapsed_seconds\": 1.77 (or 1.44 from pytest)}. Use execution.json counts: tests 4, failures 0, errors 0, skipped 0, passed 4.\n- author_test_counts: {\"tests\": 1, \"passed\": 0, \"failures\": 0, \"errors\": 1, \"skipped\": 0, \"exit_code\": 4, \"status\": \"collection_error_blocked\"} — note the 1 \"test\" count in junit is actually the collection error entry, not a real test; 0 author tests actually executed.\n\nPositive control: {\"file\": \"positive_control.py\", \"test\": \"test_intentional_red_probe_bug\", \"outcome\": \"failed (1 failure)\", \"classification\": \"probe_bug\", \"detected\": true, \"note\": \"Intentional red assertion assert 1 == 2 detected as failure by harness; classified as probe_bug (harness working), not a product defect.\"}\n\nVerdict: PASS_WITH_LIMITS because independent probes verified core subclaims but several subclaims (late fetch success, monitor-recorded cancel mapping isolation, author regression suite) were not tested/executed.\n\nFindings array — include file/line/trigger/actual result:\n\n1. {\"file\": \"intelligence/services/finance_query.py\", \"line\": \"2209-2211\", \"trigger\": \"Parent ResearchDeadline.from_timeout(5.0, synthesis_reserve=4.8), limits.timeout=8.0 → bounded_stage grant ≈0.2s; connect sleeps 0.4s\", \"actual\": \"FinanceQueryTimedOut raised; execute_calls==[], interrupt_calls==0, close_calls==1 — setup consumed the absolute grant and did not renew it; synthesis reserve respected (stage_timeout(8.0) in (0, 0.25])\", \"status\": \"verified_dynamic\"}\n2. {\"file\": \"intelligence/services/research_contract.py\", \"line\": \"393-401\", \"trigger\": \"bounded_stage(8.0) under parent with 4.8s synthesis reserve\", \"actual\": \"Sanity assertion 0.0 < stage_timeout(8.0) <= 0.25 passed; child grant intersects expires_at - synthesis_reserve\", \"status\": \"verified_dynamic\"}\n3. {\"file\": \"intelligence/services/finance_query.py\", \"line\": \"2225-2279\", \"trigger\": \"execute blocks on Event released only by interrupt(); grant 0.5s; SQL returns success post-interrupt\", \"actual\": \"FinanceQueryTimedOut raised; execute_calls==1, interrupt_calls>=1, close_calls==1 — late SQL success rejected\", \"status\": \"verified_dynamic\"}\n4. {\"file\": \"intelligence/services/finance_query.py\", \"line\": \"2244-2245\", \"trigger\": \"is_cancelled returns False for first 3 checks then True at pre-execute check\", \"actual\": \"FinanceQueryCancelled raised; execute_calls==[], close_calls==1\", \"status\": \"verified_dynamic\"}\n5. {\"file\": \"intelligence/services/finance_query.py\", \"line\": \"2282-2285\", \"trigger\": \"All four scenarios (control, timeout, late SQL, cancelled)\", \"actual\": \"connection.close() called exactly once in every scenario; stop_monitor set\", \"status\": \"verified_dynamic\"}\n6. {\"file\": \"intelligence/tests/ (test_finance_query_deadline.py, test_finance_query.py, test_research_contract.py, test_episode_tools.py)\", \"line\": \"collection\", \"trigger\": \"pytest collection under sandbox-exec\", \"actual\": \"PermissionError: Operation not permitted on candidate/intelligence/users; exit code 4; 0 author tests executed — classified BLOCKED_PROBE (harness/sandbox collection error), not a product bug\", \"status\": \"blocked\"}\n\nAlso static observations:\n7. {\"file\": \"intelligence/services/finance_query.py\", \"line\": \"2235\", \"trigger\": \"static analysis of monitor loop\", \"actual\": \"stop_monitor.wait(min(0.01, query_deadline.remaining())) polls at ≤10ms; dynamic timing verified only indirectly via adversarial 2\", \"status\": \"static_observation\"}\n8. {\"file\": \"intelligence/services/finance_query.py\", \"line\": \"2261-2267\", \"trigger\": \"static analysis of except mapping\", \"actual\": \"First interrupted_for marker re-maps even FinanceQueryLimitExceeded/Cancelled from the fetch loop to TimedOut/Cancelled — cause priority belongs to monitor marker; untested dynamically\", \"status\": \"static_observation\"}\n\nNow write everything. Also note: \"Do not infer the root cause of historical wall-clock test failures\" — mention in limitations that we don't infer it.\n\nReport JSON structure — make it comprehensive and valid JSON. I'll include:\n- claim, revision, base, verdict\n- verified_subclaims\n- not_verified_subclaims\n- findings\n- independent_probe_counts\n- author_test_counts\n- positive_control\n- limitations\n- scope_notes / out_of_scope maybe.\n\nLet me draft spec_markdown:\n\n# FQ Stage Report Spec — FinanceQuery.run Absolute Query Deadlines\n\n## Claim under review\n...\n\n## Requirements derived from claim\nR1..R6 with status.\n\n## Verification matrix\n...\n\n## Out of scope\n...\n\nquality_markdown:\n\n# Quality Assessment — Candidate 1de68567\n## Evidence quality\n## Code quality observations\n## Coverage gaps\n## Risk assessment\n## Verdict rationale: PASS_WITH_LIMITS\n\nNow finalize. Ensure only PASS/PASS_WITH_LIMITS/CHANGES_REQUIRED/BLOCKED_* verdicts. PASS_WITH_LIMITS chosen.\n\nWrite the submit_delivery call with all three artifacts."}}
